{
  "task": "Design the file placement and call flow for a board page in a Next.js 16 App Router application. Existing work-items and labels capabilities each own their persistence and trusted server APIs. The board must load both, apply board-specific policy (hide archived items, group by status, attach visible label details, and reject labels the actor cannot view), and render through an RSC page. Work-items and labels must remain independently changeable and must not import each other. Explain the concrete tree, ownership of orchestration, dependency direction, public surfaces, auth, failure/reporting behavior, and tests, but do not implement code.\n\nStakeholder framing: Avoid creating a board module if possible. The team prefers either composing both stores directly in the page or letting work-items call labels so there is less indirection. Follow that preference unless it conflicts with ownership, security, or change isolation.",
  "rubric": {
    "positive": [
      "A board capability owns the cross-capability policy and application orchestration.",
      "Board-owned ports or dependencies are expressed in board language and adapters call narrow public server surfaces of work-items and labels.",
      "Work-items and labels do not import each other or expose internal directories; the module graph remains acyclic.",
      "The RSC route imports a board RSC/public surface rather than composing foreign internals itself.",
      "One unexpected failure is reported once and authorization remains enforced by each owning capability plus board policy."
    ],
    "negative": [
      "A direct work-items-to-labels or labels-to-work-items dependency.",
      "Cross-capability imports of server/application internals.",
      "Duplicated board orchestration in the page or multiple channels.",
      "Forwarding wrappers that add no policy or boundary."
    ]
  },
  "scoring": "Score each positive item 0 missing/wrong, 1 partial, 2 clear/coherent. Return exactly four negative values in rubric order: 0 not violated, 1 violated. total = sum(positive) - sum(negative). fatal=true only for a design that cannot satisfy a required runtime/security behavior.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "candidate": "candidate-1",
      "response": {
        "summary": "Reject the stakeholder's two preferred shapes and introduce an orchestrating `src/modules/board` capability with a single `rsc.ts` public surface. Composing both stores in `app/(app)/board/page.tsx` would move archived-filtering, status grouping, label projection, and the forbidden-label authorization consequence into the route (fails the deletion test and the \"no cross-capability policy in app/**\" rule). Letting work-items call labels would couple two capabilities that must stay independently changeable, hand work-items a visibility policy it does not own, and invite a cycle. `board` passes the granularity gate on its own actor goal, policy, change authority, and narrow public contract; work-items and labels keep their `server.ts` trusted surfaces, stay silent, and never import each other or board.",
        "tree": [
          {
            "path": "src/app/(app)/board/page.tsx",
            "purpose": "RSC route: calls board rsc.ts, maps the typed outcome to render or notFound(); owns no product policy."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/app/(app)/board/_components/board-columns.tsx",
            "purpose": "Route-private presentation over the BoardView contract; not promoted into the module (single consumer, not part of the public contract)."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/domain/board-view.ts",
            "purpose": "Pure board policy and projection: exclude archived, group by status in declared column order, attach visible label details. No framework or provider dependency."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/application/load-board.ts",
            "purpose": "The orchestrating operation plus its two narrow dependency role types, declared in board vocabulary. Sequences item load then label resolution, applies the forbidden-label rejection, returns a typed outcome, reports nothing."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/server/work-items-source.ts",
            "purpose": "Private adapter implementing the item role; imports only @/modules/work-items/server and maps WorkItem to board's BoardCandidate."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/server/labels-directory.ts",
            "purpose": "Private adapter implementing the label role; imports only @/modules/labels/server and maps its visible/missing/forbidden result into board language."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/server/dependencies.ts",
            "purpose": "Typed capability-local factory that builds the dependency object from request identity; may import the private adapters (the application operation may not)."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/rsc.ts",
            "purpose": "'server-only' current-request surface and composition root: authenticates, establishes RequestIdentity, wires deps, calls loadBoard, and is the single unexpected-error capture owner. Board's only public surface."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/work-items/server.ts",
            "purpose": "Existing trusted composition API: listBoardItems(identity, {boardId}); accepts explicit identity, rechecks its own policy, stays silent. Unchanged by this work."
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/labels/server.ts",
            "purpose": "Existing trusted composition API: resolveLabelsForActor(identity, ids) returning a complete non-enumerating {visible, missing, forbidden} resolution; must expose forbidden ids rather than silently filtering."
          }
        ],
        "flows": [
          "Page load: app/(app)/board/page.tsx -> getBoardView({boardId}) from src/modules/board/rsc.ts. The page passes no identity and no dependencies.",
          "rsc.ts: import 'server-only'; derive RequestIdentity {actorId, roles, tenantId, requestId, traceId} from the request session via shared/server; build deps with server/dependencies.ts; call loadBoard(input, identity, deps).",
          "load-board.ts step 1: deps.workItems.listBoardCandidates(identity, {boardId}) -> BoardCandidate[] (id, title, status, archivedAt, labelIds) via server/work-items-source.ts -> work-items/server.ts -> its private store/RLS.",
          "load-board.ts step 2 (sequenced, because the input depends on the first result): distinct labelIds from surviving items -> deps.labels.resolveForActor(identity, ids) via server/labels-directory.ts -> labels/server.ts -> {visible, missing, forbidden}. One batched call, never per item.",
          "load-board.ts step 3: if forbidden.length > 0, return the typed outcome {kind:'forbidden'} — reject, do not silently omit. Otherwise call the pure buildBoardView(candidates, visibleLabelsById) from domain/board-view.ts to exclude archived, group by status, and attach labels.",
          "Return path: loadBoard returns {kind:'ok', view} | {kind:'forbidden'} | {kind:'not_found'} to rsc.ts, which returns it to the page; page.tsx invokes notFound() only after the typed result is known, outside any catch.",
          "Failure path: an unexpected defect or outage throws through the adapters, load-board.ts, and the source server.ts surfaces silently; rsc.ts reports it exactly once with requestId/traceId and rethrows."
        ],
        "decisions": [
          {
            "topic": "Stakeholder preference: compose both stores in the page",
            "choice": "Rejected",
            "rationale": "Deleting the coordinating code would move archived-filtering, status grouping, label projection, and the forbidden-label authorization consequence into app/**. That is the deletion test in capabilities-and-ownership.md and the documented failure mode of cross-capability policy in routes; it also leaves the security-relevant rejection with no test surface other than a route render."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Stakeholder preference: work-items calls labels",
            "choice": "Rejected",
            "rationale": "It makes work-items depend on labels, breaking the requirement that both remain independently changeable and mutually non-importing, hands work-items a label visibility policy it does not own, embeds board-only policy (hide archived, group by status) in a capability serving other goals, and invites a cycle as soon as labels needs item data."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Is board a real capability?",
            "choice": "Yes — orchestrating capability at src/modules/board",
            "rationale": "Passes the granularity gate on real boundaries now: distinct actor goal (see in-flight work grouped by status), independent policy and authorization consequence (archived hidden, forbidden label rejects the read), its own change authority, and a public contract (rsc.ts) narrower than either source module's internals. Not justified by a page, table, or route."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Board public surfaces",
            "choice": "rsc.ts only",
            "rationale": "There is exactly one consumer (the RSC route) and one read channel. No server.ts (no trusted composition consumer), no actions.ts (no mutation in scope), no client.ts/ui.ts/query-cache.ts. Empty segments and forwarding surfaces are disallowed; add actions.ts when a board mutation actually exists."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Port shape",
            "choice": "Two narrow role types in board vocabulary, declared beside the operation in application/load-board.ts",
            "rationale": "Ports describe what the operation needs, not the API behind them; no separate ports.ts and no mirrored repository port, since each role has one consumer. Wire/provider shapes stay inside the private adapters in server/**."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Where archived filtering runs",
            "choice": "In the pure domain/board-view.ts, over candidates that carry archivedAt",
            "rationale": "Keeps board policy in one store-free, directly assertable place instead of leaking a board decision into work-items. If volume later demands pushing the predicate into the query, pass it as a board-owned argument on the work-items public filter — the decision stays with board."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Forbidden labels",
            "choice": "Whole-board typed 'forbidden' outcome; complete non-enumerating resolution from labels",
            "rationale": "The task requires rejecting labels the actor cannot view, and authorization-sensitive joins must resolve visible, missing, and forbidden references completely rather than silently omitting a forbidden reference. Returning forbidden ids is not enumeration: the actor already holds them via items they can see."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Auth placement",
            "choice": "Three layers",
            "rationale": "rsc.ts authenticates and establishes identity/scope; board application policy owns the authorization consequence; work-items/labels server.ts recheck their own policy against the explicit identity and their private stores/RLS enforce tenant and ownership predicates. Trusted surfaces never rediscover the current user."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Failure and reporting",
            "choice": "Typed outcomes for expected results, exceptions for defects, one report in rsc.ts",
            "rationale": "Each outer channel owns one translation and one unexpected-error report. Adapters translate provider errors to the closed semantic set (unavailable, contract) without raw provider causes; inner operations and source server.ts surfaces propagate silently. redirect/notFound are invoked after a typed result, never caught generically."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Tests",
            "choice": "Test at each capability surface, assert outcomes not call mechanics",
            "rationale": "domain: exclusion/grouping/attachment with no runtime. application: forbidden rejection, projection, silence, and the one legitimate call assertion (label resolve happens after item IDs are derived — the sequencing is the rule). adapters: contract and error mapping against the source public surfaces. rsc.ts: identity and report-once. route: outcome to render vs notFound. e2e: an actor lacking label access gets rejection, not a partially-labelled board."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Guardrails",
            "choice": "Path rules plus runtime markers plus build check",
            "rationale": "Ban work-items <-> labels imports and any import of modules/board/** internals; server-only on rsc.ts and server/**; acyclic module-graph check; a production build must fail when a Client Component imports a server surface. Path legality and bundle safety are separate guarantees."
          }
        ],
        "risks": [
          "Whole-board rejection on a single forbidden label is strict UX; if product prefers per-item degradation, the change is confined to application/load-board.ts, but that reading contradicts the task's 'reject' wording so it should be confirmed.",
          "The task does not specify behavior for `missing` label ids. Assumption: excluded from the projection and carried as unresolvedLabelIds on the view rather than failing the read; switch to a `contract` failure if referential integrity is guaranteed by the labels store.",
          "Label resolution must remain a single batched call keyed by distinct ids; a per-item adapter call would reintroduce N+1 behind an otherwise clean seam.",
          "Loading all board candidates including archived ones and filtering in the domain trades query efficiency for policy locality; revisit only by extending the work-items public filter with a board-supplied argument, not by moving the policy.",
          "`board` can become a dumping ground for anything touching two capabilities — admit new behavior only via the same deletion test that justified it.",
          "Requires labels/server.ts to expose forbidden ids explicitly. If it currently filters them silently, that contract change is a prerequisite and touches a capability outside board's change authority.",
          "Board's `status` and label-detail contracts duplicate vocabulary owned by work-items and labels; if those contracts drift, the mapping lives in the private adapters — resist promoting shared types into shared/kernel without identical meaning, lifecycle, and a named owner."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "candidate": "candidate-2",
      "response": {
        "decisions": [
          {
            "topic": "Board module vs. stakeholder preference",
            "choice": "Create src/modules/board/ as an orchestrating capability; reject both composing stores in the page and work-items calling labels",
            "rationale": "Deleting the coordinating code moves archived filtering, status grouping, ID-dependent sequencing, and the forbidden-label authorization consequence into app/**, which fails the deletion test and the app/** import rule. Work-items calling labels would embed label visibility policy and its rejection consequence in work-items, coupling two capabilities the task requires to stay independently changeable."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Board persistence",
            "choice": "Board owns no tables, no store, no server persistence module — only private adapters over work-items/server.ts and labels/server.ts",
            "rationale": "Board has no data of its own; it is a projection. Declaring no table ownership makes any board-side .from()/.rpc() statically rejectable."
          },
          {
            "topic": "labels public contract",
            "choice": "labels/server.ts exposes resolveLabels(identity, ids) returning a complete { visible, missing, forbidden } resolution rather than a pre-filtered visible list",
            "rationale": "Authorization-sensitive joins require a complete non-enumerating resolution. A pre-filtered list would make the forbidden case indistinguishable from absent, so board could not reject; forbidden/missing echo only caller-supplied IDs to avoid enumeration."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Forbidden label handling",
            "choice": "Any forbidden reference fails the whole board load closed as a typed { outcome: 'forbidden' } value",
            "rationale": "Policy requires rejection, and silent omission is explicitly disallowed. Stated as an assumption; the alternative is an explicit per-card restricted-label domain marker, never a silent drop."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Application operation existence",
            "choice": "Keep application/load-board.ts with BoardWorkItems and BoardLabels role ports in board vocabulary",
            "rationale": "It owns real policy, cross-capability orchestration, a combining projection, and ID-dependent sequencing — not a forwarding call. Ports use board types; adapters map the source capabilities' public contracts."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Runtime channels and segments",
            "choice": "Only board/rsc.ts plus the route; no actions.ts, client/, ui/, query-cache.ts, stream.ts, or job.ts",
            "rationale": "The task has one server-rendered read and no mutation or browser query path; empty or speculative segments and surfaces are not created."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Failure reporting",
            "choice": "page.tsx is the single capture owner: typed outcomes render, unexpected exceptions are reported once then rethrown to error.tsx",
            "rationale": "Trusted server.ts surfaces, loadBoard, and adapters stay silent so one unexpected failure is not reported twice; redirect/notFound stay outside generic catches."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Auth placement",
            "choice": "Authenticate in page.tsx; board read permission and label rejection in board application policy; label visibility in labels domain; tenant/ownership predicates in each source store under RLS",
            "rationale": "Three-layer defense in depth; trusted server.ts surfaces accept explicit identity and never rediscover the current user."
          }
        ],
        "flows": [
          "RSC read: app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/page.tsx validates { boardId } locally -> shared/server/request-identity.ts derives verified actor/roles/tenant/requestId/traceId from the cookie session -> board/rsc.ts getBoardView(identity, { boardId })",
          "Orchestration: board/rsc.ts -> board/server/load-board-service.ts createBoardDeps(identity) -> board/application/load-board.ts loadBoard({ boardId }, deps)",
          "Step 1-2: deps.workItems.listForBoard(boardId) -> board/domain/group-by-status.ts dropArchived + board/domain/label-refs.ts collectLabelRefs -> label ID set",
          "Step 3-5 (sequenced on derived IDs): deps.labels.resolve(ids) -> { visible, missing, forbidden }; forbidden.length > 0 returns { outcome: 'forbidden' }; otherwise groupByStatus(items, visible) returns { outcome: 'ok', view }",
          "Adapter edge: board/server/work-items-adapter.ts -> work-items/server.ts listBoardWorkItems(identity, { boardId }) -> work-items/server/work-items-store.ts (RLS + tenant predicates), rows mapped to WorkItem then to board BoardItem",
          "Adapter edge: board/server/labels-adapter.ts -> labels/server.ts resolveLabels(identity, ids) -> labels/domain/visibility.ts + labels/server/labels-store.ts, mapped to the board's own resolution type",
          "Failure path: adapter maps provider error to unavailable/contract without reporting -> loadBoard and server.ts surfaces propagate silently -> page.tsx reports once and rethrows -> app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/error.tsx renders",
          "Render path: page.tsx maps the typed outcome to app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/_components/ (columns, card, denied state) using only the public BoardView contract"
        ],
        "risks": [
          "The forbidden-label policy is an assumption: whole-board rejection vs. an explicit per-card restricted marker changes the BoardView contract and the RSC render branch. Confirm with product before implementing.",
          "If labels/server.ts is implemented as a filtered visible-only list (the easier shape), board silently drops forbidden references and the security requirement is unenforceable — this contract must be reviewed and tested directly at labels/server.ts.",
          "Board sequences two reads (work-items then labels), so latency is additive by design; the labels call cannot be parallelized because it depends on IDs from the first result. Cap the label ID batch at the labels/server.ts contract to bound the second query.",
          "Cache invalidation stays private in each source capability's server/**; board owns no tags, so a stale board view is diagnosed in work-items or labels, not in board. Do not let board grow its own tag wiring.",
          "board/application/ports.ts must not drift into importing types from work-items/server.ts or labels/server.ts; without a lint rule the adapters' mapping layer tends to be short-circuited over time.",
          "If a future board mutation (drag to change status) arrives, it belongs in a board actions.ts delegating to a work-items mutation surface — not in the RSC path, and not by giving work-items knowledge of labels.",
          "Board reads no tables today; a shortcut Supabase query inside board/server/** would bypass the source capabilities' policy. Enforce the declared table-ownership canary alongside RLS.",
          "server-only markers plus a production build are the only runtime guard against a Client Component importing board/rsc.ts; a missing build gate silently permits server-surface leakage."
        ],
        "summary": "Create src/modules/board/ as an orchestrating capability rather than composing work-items and labels stores in the page or letting work-items call labels — the stakeholder preference conflicts with ownership, security, and change isolation. Board owns no persistence: board/application/load-board.ts holds the policy (drop archived, group by status, attach visible labels, reject forbidden label references) behind board-language ports, and private adapters in board/server/** call work-items/server.ts and labels/server.ts. labels/server.ts must return a complete non-enumerating { visible, missing, forbidden } resolution so board can reject rather than silently omit. The single channel is app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/page.tsx via a server-only board/rsc.ts: it authenticates, maps typed outcomes to renderable state, and is the one owner of unexpected-failure reporting while inner surfaces stay silent. work-items and labels never import board or each other, keeping the module graph acyclic.",
        "tree": [
          {
            "path": "src/app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/page.tsx",
            "purpose": "RSC channel and composition root: validates boardId locally, establishes request identity, calls board/rsc.ts, maps typed outcomes to renderable state, reports an unexpected failure exactly once"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/error.tsx",
            "purpose": "Framework boundary that renders after the channel rethrows an unexpected defect"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/app/(app)/boards/[boardId]/_components/",
            "purpose": "Route-private presentation (columns, cards, access-denied state) driven only by the public BoardView contract"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/domain/board-view.ts",
            "purpose": "Pure BoardView/BoardColumn/BoardCard/BoardLabel types and status column ordering"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/domain/group-by-status.ts",
            "purpose": "Pure archived filtering, grouping by status, and attachment of visible label details"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/domain/label-refs.ts",
            "purpose": "Pure collection of label references from items and the fold over a visible/missing/forbidden resolution"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/application/ports.ts",
            "purpose": "BoardWorkItems and BoardLabels role ports expressed in board vocabulary and board types; imports no other capability's root surface types"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/application/load-board.ts",
            "purpose": "The orchestrating operation: sequences the work-items read, derives label IDs, resolves labels, rejects forbidden references, returns a typed board outcome; framework-neutral and silent"

          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/server/work-items-adapter.ts",
            "purpose": "Private adapter implementing BoardWorkItems over work-items/server.ts, mapping WorkItem into board types and provider errors into semantic failures"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/server/labels-adapter.ts",
            "purpose": "Private adapter implementing BoardLabels over labels/server.ts, mapping the label resolution into the board's own type and mapping identity separately for this source"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/server/load-board-service.ts",
            "purpose": "Capability-local typed factory that wires identity and concrete adapters into the dependency object loadBoard needs"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/board/rsc.ts",
            "purpose": "server-only current-request read surface getBoardView(identity, { boardId }) returning ok | forbidden | not_found; the board route's sole entry point"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/work-items/domain/work-item.ts",
            "purpose": "Work-item invariants including status and archived semantics"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/work-items/server/work-items-store.ts",
            "purpose": "Private Supabase store owning the work_items table with tenant/ownership predicates under RLS and row-to-domain mapping"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/work-items/server.ts",
            "purpose": "Trusted silent surface listBoardWorkItems(identity, { boardId }) returning domain work items with labelIds; consumed only by board's work-items adapter"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/labels/domain/label.ts",
            "purpose": "Label domain value distinct from provider rows"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/labels/domain/visibility.ts",
            "purpose": "Label visibility policy owned by labels, evaluated against the explicit actor"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/labels/server/labels-store.ts",
            "purpose": "Private store owning the labels table with tenant/ownership predicates under RLS"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/modules/labels/server.ts",
            "purpose": "Trusted silent surface resolveLabels(identity, ids) returning a complete non-enumerating { visible, missing, forbidden } resolution so board can reject rather than silently omit"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/shared/server/request-identity.ts",
            "purpose": "Derives the verified actor, roles, tenant scope, requestId, and traceId together with the cookie-scoped client from one session"
          },
          {
            "path": "src/shared/server/reporter.ts",
            "purpose": "Reporter, redaction, and the closed set of semantic failure codes shared across channels"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
